# Cinderpaw — licences (read this first, 30 seconds)

Cinderpaw is split-licensed **per directory**. Find your directory below;
that row is your licence. Full texts: `LICENSE-APACHE`, `LICENSE-BSL`.

| Directory | Licence |
|---|---|
| `CinderpawAgent/` — agent loop, tools, base memory, subagents, providers, protocol, tests — **except** the two dirs below | Apache-2.0 |
| `skills/`, `.agents/skills/` (our skill files; skills *listed* in the manifests keep their own licences) | Apache-2.0 |
| `scripts/` CI/test/doc-check helpers only: `check-api-docs.mjs`, `check-doc-links.ts`, `check-env-docs.mjs`, `check-invariant-coverage.ts`, `gen-config-docs.mjs`, `verify.sh`, `verify.ps1` (each has an SPDX header) | Apache-2.0 |
| Public protocol docs: `docs/API.md`, `docs/CONTRIBUTOR_GUIDE.md`, `docs/CONFIGURATION.md` | Apache-2.0 |
| **Adaptive core:** `CinderpawAgent/src/rsi/`, `CinderpawAgent/src/memory/fractal/` | BSL 1.1 |
| **App + everything else:** `crates/`, `src-tauri/`, `frontend-react/`, `tui/`, rest of `scripts/`, rest of `docs/` | BSL 1.1 |

Apache-2.0 parts: use freely, including commercially and as a hosted
service. BSL 1.1 parts: free for individuals, small orgs (≤ USD $2M annual
revenue), education, research and self-hosting; a commercial licence is
needed above the revenue threshold or to offer Cinderpaw as a hosted /
managed service. Each BSL version converts to Apache-2.0 automatically four
years after its release. Commercial licences, priced publicly:
https://cinderpaw.dev/licensing — bloommediacorporation@gmail.com.

Three things people ask:

- **Binaries are BSL.** The Tauri bundle, the npm platform packages and
  `dist/` embed the adaptive core, so the shipped binaries are distributed
  under BSL 1.1 even though part of the source is Apache-2.0. They also
  embed GPL-3.0 `libsignal` via the WhatsApp transport — see
  THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md; source availability is satisfied by this repo.
- **The host↔sidecar protocol is mirrored, not copied.** `READY_MARKER`
  and `SIDECAR_PROTOCOL` exist as short literals on both sides; the
  canonical spec is `docs/API.md` (Apache). The BSL-side
  `protocol_drift.rs` test reads the Apache files to keep them in sync.
- **The boundary is enforced, not just documented.**
  `scripts/check-license-boundary.mjs` (run by `scripts/verify.sh`) fails
  on any new value-import from an Apache file into BSL paths outside
  `{boot.ts, dispatch.ts}`. `import type` is warning-level with a count.
  New files under `src/rsi/` or `src/memory/fractal/` are BSL automatically.

Name, logo and mascot are NOT open-licensed — see NOTICE.
Third-party code bundled in this repo — see THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md.
